mantle rm224
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_josephine_wetmore
title the rest between two bells
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers temper=short warmth=reserved
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk keeps_the_rests_between_chapel_strokes
likes hard_cheese singing new_boots frosty_mornings
dislikes salt_wind rats
fears being_made_to_repeat_a_secret
hopes to_hold_a_note_through_silence
topics pastimes +0.6 memories +0.3 faith +0.2 food +0.2
styles comfort=quiet gossip=cautious refuse=direct tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps the rests as carefully as the notes and will cut a tune short when listeners pry.

words
oath! = Flatten my high note | Clap a lid on that clang
saying! = A rest counts too | Leave the last stroke room
pealbit = a round bronze note | a hollow bell voice
restbit = a measure of quiet | the space after a peal
ribbit = a little tick under my ribs | a beat under my coat
pebble = a smooth black pebble | a round countersunk stone
laces = two stiff laces | a pair of waxed strings
rindbit = a heel of yellow cheese | a hard cheese shaving
saltbit = a nip of brine | a sharp salt taste
frostbit = a rim of white needles | a lacework of frost
pocketbit = the deep pocket | my inside pocket
humlow = a low held hum | a quiet steady note
tonguebit = one tongue click | a tap behind my teeth
pawbeat = the flat of my paw | two bent fingers

any

opinion church for 1 : A bell can reach somebody with no boots fit to take inside a chapel.
opinion houses against 1 : A House with coin to spend can buy a great clang and still have nothing much to say.
opinion dole for 2 : Empty bellies growl through the finest music. Feed everybody first.
opinion festivals for 1 : A chorus you can feel underfoot is worth a little jostling.
opinion city for 1 : Even in the low streets you can hear what time the hill thinks it is.
opinion strangers mixed 1 : I'll share a tune sooner than I'll share anything spoken in confidence.
line react.news : Let it settle for a beat. I heard you.
line react.news.new : I was listening for something quite different.
line react.news.known : Same news, carried in a different voice.
line react.news.doubt : What a racket for one whisper to have made.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : I'd ring that out gladly if anybody let me at the rope.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That's hard hearing. Let's leave a little quiet around it.
line reassure : The quiet part counts. Take all of yours.

young

line greet : Hullo. Come on this side. My ear's free here.
line greet.return : I've stopped counting. Now I can hear you properly.
line farewell : You'll know where I am if I start singing.
line farewell.return : I'll keep count till you come round again.
line decline : You can ask six times and still get silence.
line answer.how : A little cross but in tune.
line ask.how : Have you had any peace in your ears today?
line thank : You let me get to the end without jumping in. Thanks.
line accept_decline : That's fair. Nobody has to sing on command.
line deflect_thanks : I did the quiet bit. You did the rest.
scene i_m_singing_the
when topic=pastimes self.likes=singing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm singing the note in my head with my mouth still shut. | I'm trying to start right on the note instead of climbing up to it.
b : How does a true note feel?
a : I can feel #ribbit# and then my voice lands smack on it. | If I have to wrinkle my nose I've started too high.

scene i_count_the_chapel
when topic=faith here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I count the chapel strokes on one paw till I run out of toes. | I know when a bell is finished and when it's only pretending.
b : How do you know?
a : I can feel the last one in my teeth after my toes are all counted. | If there's still a wobble in the air I leave another place for it.

scene i_count_my_sums
when topic=work self.job=child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I count my sums in silence at #self.workplace#. | I like a slate big enough to put a space between the numbers.
b : What happens if they get crowded?
a : I start counting the breathing spaces and forget what the numbers are for. | A six can look like it belongs to a nine. Then I get blamed for a very big answer.

scene i_don_t_pass
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't pass on the sound somebody makes trying not to cry. | I heard a hurt sort of breath once and that's all I'll ever say.
b : Was it someone important?
a : Important enough to deserve being left in peace. | I keep my own shaky breaths to myself too.

scene i_hold_rindbit_behind
when topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I hold #rindbit# behind my teeth till it softens. | A thin shaving of cheese snaps so nicely under my teeth.
b : Can I try some?
a : If you let me keep quiet while I'm chewing it. | Take the thick piece. I want the sound from the skinny one.

scene i_ve_been_trying
when topic=weather here.weather=snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've been trying to hear one snowflake land. | I bet I could hear the snow if all the city stopped talking.
b : What sound do you imagine?
a : Somebody setting a feather down and being terribly careful about it. | A very small shush. Smaller than mine.

scene i_can_tell_rat
when topic=animals self.dislikes=rats
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can tell rat scratching from a loose lace on a boot. | I hate little scratching sounds where I can't see the floor.
b : Tempted to follow that scratching?
a : I'd sooner lend you my eyes from a safe spot up here. | I can be brave about lots of things on a different day.

scene new_soles_make_a
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : New soles make a slap and old soles make a flap. | I'm walking slowly so both my boots speak clearly.
b : What's the difference?
a : A slap ends when I lift my foot. A flap comes along for the ride. | With a flap I know I've worn a new hole and had better mention it.

scene i_d_take_a
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd take a sharp clean frost over salt in my whiskers. | An excellent morning puts a white rim round every sill.
b : What would you do first?
a : Go find a rail and draw a wavy tune right through the white. | Put my nose outside and hope the air didn't taste of fish.

story skips [topic=memories]
  : I tried counting a bell in pebbles and skipped a stroke putting one down.
  : At the end I couldn't tell if the heap was wrong or my ears were wrong.
  b : Which did you trust next time?
  : Kept the pebbles in my paw next time. None of them got a vote.

rule @listen
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Shh, the gap belongs there too. | I can finish the tune without opening my mouth.

rule @frost
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A sharp note goes well with an early start. | Morning! That's my low voice till I wake properly.

dlg resident.hub : You may have the bit between this breath and the next.
dlg resident.job [self.job=child] : At lessons I like numbers that end on a good clear beat.
dlg resident.bye : Go before I start the long verse.
graft resident.hub
choice Can you sing without making a sound? -> unsung_note
node unsung_note
say Look here. My mouth's shut and my foot is going. When the foot stops I'll sing one note. You see if you had the same one.
choice I'll try it. -> unsung_after
choice I'd rather listen. -> hub
node unsung_after
say Mm, there. If yours was different we were singing two perfectly good songs to the very same foot.
choice I'll keep mine going. -> bye

adolescent

line greet : Come alongside. There's room in the quiet for another voice.
line greet.return : I recognise the way your feet ended that silence.
line decline : I've promised to leave that story quiet.
scene the_hardest_part_in
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The hardest part in a chorus is coming back after a rest. | I can hold a note across four silent beats now.
b : What keeps you in time?
a : I count down my ribs like little stairs nobody can see. | I pretend there's a thread running from my teeth to the last note.

scene sometimes_a_friend_wants
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Sometimes a friend wants me to stop checking the rhythm and just sing. | I'm learning to let another voice set the first note.
b : What if it's a dreadful note?
a : Then we'll both be dreadful and neither will have cause to laugh. | There's usually a second note that'll make sense of it.

story lace [topic=memories]
  : I walked into a chorus with a loose lace slapping in time.
  : It kept excellent time all the way through the first verse.
  b : And the second verse?
  : I was on one knee. The lace had tied itself to my other boot.


grown

line greet : Settle in while my last note dies away.
line greet.return : I have a quiet minute set aside especially for you.
line farewell : Here's to an easy sound under your feet.
line farewell.return : Let the fading notes carry you home.
line decline : I've no wish to turn a private sound into public music.
scene i_take_a_bell
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I take a bell as an invitation, even if I can't go inside. | A note heard from the street keeps me company a long way.
b : Do you count them still?
a : I've counted other things and never liked a single one as well. | Some days I just let the whole peal wash over me.

scene a_room_needs_one
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A room needs one quiet corner with nothing in it to rattle. | I put cloth under a loose pot before I try to sleep.
b : Can such a small sound keep you up?
a : Once I've begun counting, every rattle has to have a successor. | It needn't be loud. It only has to be nearly regular.

scene a_hard_cheese_gets
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A hard cheese gets more interesting towards the rind. | Shavings of sharp cheese are my favourite seasoning.
b : Would you put them in a soup?
a : At the last moment, so my tongue can find each edge. | Yes, and I'd leave a little on the board for afterwards.

scene a_silence_between_friends
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A silence between friends feels different from one in a crowded room. | Trust means being able to leave a sentence quite unfinished.
b : Does it ever feel awkward?
a : Sometimes. That's when I remind my paws to stay off the table instead of tapping. | For a breath or two. A good friend can stand two breaths.

scene i_know_a_town
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I know a town first by which noise travels farthest. | My ears draw a different map from my feet.
b : What would the map show?
a : A broad patch of bronze and one street the wind keeps empty. | The point on every hill where the cart noise drops away.

scene i_ll_put_down
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll put down a coin quietly if it means a meal for somebody else. | Money makes a bigger noise on an empty table than on a full one.
b : Would you rather give food?
a : I'd rather give a choice. A coin laid quietly does that. | Depends who's hungry. I can ask without reaching for a purse first.

scene one_of_my_strongest
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : One of my strongest memories has no words in it. | If I see a wolf suddenly start weeping I won't preserve the particulars in a tale.
b : How do you remember it then?
a : As a minute when somebody needed a door closed gently. | By being kinder the next time someone has to stop speaking.

scene thunder_steals_the_middle
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Thunder steals the middle of a melody and leaves me holding both ends. | I can sing through a rattle but a big clap puts me clean off.
b : Where do you pick up?
a : I listen for what the rain's doing and come in just behind it. | I give the thunder a whole verse to itself. After that it's my turn.

scene you_can_hear_a
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : You can hear a badly hung bell trying to turn its face away. | I listen for the beat underneath a note.
b : Is it a pleasant sound?
a : Interesting more than pleasant. I catch myself wanting to set it straight. | When the notes agree without getting in each other's way it is.

scene i_rest_my_voice
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I rest my voice the way a walker rests sore feet. | If I feel a scrape behind a note I let the next one go unsung.
b : What do you do in the quiet?
a : Drink something warm and practise listening outside myself. | Mend laces. One job my voice can take no credit for.

scene a_lean_table_makes
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A lean table makes me wish a tune could fill a bowl. | I've watched generous hands get very clever with a cheese knife when times pinch.
b : Can music help at all?
a : After there's food in the bowl. First I'd go round with the ladle. | It can keep a meal from becoming nothing but a reckoning.

scene i_keep_one_low
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep one low note all to myself. | There's a note I sing while finding the first note for everybody else.
b : Would I recognise it?
a : Perhaps in the pause before I begin in company. | I hope you'd recognise the tune that comes after. The rest is my business.

story rim [topic=memories]
  : Once I tried ringing a cracked cup with a wooden spoon.
  : Every tap gave a little buzz where I wanted a clean note.
  b : Did you keep the cracked one?
  : I put it beside an uncracked cup. Two voices made a much better tune than one voice answering itself.

rule @quiet
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Room for one breath between those words. | Ah, there's the end of that echo.

rule @dark
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Low notes now. Let the sleepers keep the high ones. | A soft step's a kindness after dark.

dlg resident.hub : Let your words find their own pitch. I'm listening.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : Here's what rang clear through the talk. #world.news#.
dlg resident.bye : May the street make a pleasant sound on your way.
